+# Skill: ORC and Orchestration Lab Session Coherence Guard
+
+Run at the end of a work session, before commit or handoff. Check only this session's change.
+
+## Modes and safety
+- Follow the invocation's mode: plan, audit-only and discuss-first inspect and report without editing; build permits
+  scoped repairs.
+- Never commit or push unless asked. Never read, print or write secret values; inspect examples and key names instead.
+- Leave unrelated changes alone, and keep committed workflow logic out of vendor-specific agent folders.
+
+## Where things live
+- Authorised intent: lab `SCOPE.md`, `scope.yaml`, `decisions/`, `memory/authority-rules-step-1.md` and the north star
+  in `STATE.md`; ORC `README.md` ("Direction", "Boundary") and `AGENTS.md`. Steward: Justin (`scope.yaml`).
+- Current state and next steps: lab `STATE.md`. Read it first.
+- Decisions: lab `decisions/`; issue-level ones on their issues, all on the map orchestrator#140. Open: whether
+  decisions about ORC itself belong in ORC's repository (lab `decisions/2026-10-07-proposals-from-entropy-assessment.md`, P5).
+- Rules owned elsewhere: `~/pro/local-config/home/AGENTS.md`; ORC `SECURITY-REVIEW.md` and `dangerfile.js`; the map's
+  rules in orchestrator#140; `~/pro/agentic/HOW_NOT_TO_PLAN.md`; `~/pro/scope/docs/MODEL.md`.
+
+Here "lab" is `~/scopes/scope-orchestration-lab`, and "ORC" is the checkout or worktree of `~/pro/orchestrator` the
+session worked in.
+
+## What changed this session
+Find the commit the session started from, and write it in place of `<start>` below. If you cannot, use `origin/main`
+and report "coverage incomplete". If neither exists, report committed changes as not covered, and still inspect staged,
+unstaged and untracked work. Run this in each repository the session touched.
+```bash
+git log --oneline <start>..HEAD           # commits
+git diff <start> HEAD                     # what they changed
+git status --short
+git diff --cached                         # staged: what the next commit holds
+git diff                                  # unstaged
+git ls-files --others --exclude-standard  # untracked: read those that matter
+```
+<!-- Check staged and unstaged separately: `git diff HEAD` nets them out, so a change staged and then undone in the
+working tree shows nothing yet still lands. Add live changes the checks depend on (a deployed build, a grant), read
+with the time. -->
+Live changes: what ORC runs (`pnpm service:status`), cards approved and grants made this session, each read with the time.
+
+## Intent
+Does this change fit the authorised intent in the files above? If not:
+
+> When this session's work and the authorised intent disagree:
+>
+> 1. Decide which it is: a defect in the work, an adaptation within what is already authorised, or a change of
+>    intent nobody has decided.
+> 2. Fix a defect in the work.
+> 3. Go ahead with an adaptation within existing authorisation, and record its reason where that helps. Record an
+>    undecided change of intent as a proposal for Justin in the lab's `decisions/`; work that depends on it waits
+>    for the decision.
+> 4. Do not edit the intent documents listed under "Where things live" to match the work unless Justin has recorded
+>    that decision.
+> 5. Correct a document directly only when a recorded decision of Justin's already settles it, and cite that
+>    decision.
+> 6. Before making a description, an implementation and a check agree, establish which of them is wrong. A test or
+>    the code shows what is checked or built; it does not authorise weakening a documented constraint.
+
+(Intent-change rule v2, from entropy-guard: `skills/entropy-assessment/intent-change-rule.md`.)
+
+## Checks
+- If an ORC module changed what it does: do its own header (Owns / Never / Today), and any line about it in ORC
+  `README.md` or `AGENTS.md`, still describe it? `pnpm codemap --today` lists the headers.
+- For each state claim changed in lab `STATE.md`: do its other mentions, there, in `decisions/` and in ORC's docs,
+  still agree?
+- If ORC's `src/`, `package.json` or a connector changed what ORC launches or contacts (`child_process`, `.launch(`,
+  `fetch`, `node:http`, `node:https`, `node:net`, `node:dns`, `WebSocket`, `.goto(`, a new dependency that opens a
+  process or socket): do the subprocess and network lists in ORC `AGENTS.md` name it, including reach delegated to a
+  library, Pi, an MCP server or a package, and would `test/architecture.test.ts` fail if it moved? A reach no
+  recorded decision covers goes to Justin as a proposal, not into the list.
+- If lab `STATE.md` changed: is it within the cap in lab `AGENTS.md` ("Keeping state")? Does each live fact (what ORC
+  runs, grants, test counts) say when and where it was read? Does `node tools/map.mjs` still mark the
+  `**Where we are now:**` issue with ★?
+- If Justin decided something this session: is it in lab `decisions/`, or on the issue that owns it, dated and in his
+  words, and not only in `STATE.md`?
+- If ORC's durable-work store (`src/adapters/async-store/sqlite.ts`), its state directory or `src/core/*.md` changed:
+  do lab `tools/collect.mjs`'s readers still find them? They return nothing rather than fail.
+- If the session opened issues: are they on the map? `node tools/map.mjs --check` covers only the repositories in
+  `tools/collect.mjs` and passes when a read fails; check any other repository's issue on GitHub.
+- Before reviving or citing an ORC root report (`REWORK.md`, `SEAM.md`, `OPERATOR.md`, `FIXES.md` and the like) or a
+  dated lab report: does `STATE.md`, ORC `README.md` or `AGENTS.md` still treat it as current?
+- If a connector's configuration or credential names changed in ORC: does every package manifest that declares it
+  use the new names (orchestrator#198)?
+- If a path in ORC `dangerfile.js` `GUARDED` changed: is it going through a pull request, not a direct push to `main`,
+  which Danger never sees?
+```bash
+# ORC, if it changed. CI runs only Danger.
+pnpm typecheck && pnpm test
+pnpm test:e2e      # only if web/ or the durable-work surface changed
+# lab
+node tools/map.mjs --check
+node --input-type=module -e "const m = await import('./tools/collect.mjs'); console.log((await m.durableWork()) ? 'durable work read' : 'durable work NOT read', m.agents().length, 'agents')"
+grep -cv '^\s*$' STATE.md   # against the cap in AGENTS.md
+```
+
+## Repairs
+- One owner per concept: when two places define one concept independently, reduce one to a link. Keep summaries,
+  generated projections, versioned copies and independent tests, and keep them correct.
+- Limit every correction by its evidence. Change only what the evidence settles, and leave open parts visibly open.
+  For an exhaustive list or an "only" claim, check the full scope, including delegated behaviour. Never change a
+  prescribed boundary because of observed behaviour, and never treat a test or the code as the record: where a
+  description, the code and a check disagree, establish which is wrong first.
+
+## Report
+- Baseline, and whether coverage was complete; what was checked and what was not.
+- Findings caused by this session, judged by the relationship changed, not the file edited: renaming a setting in
+  the code makes an untouched README wrong. Problems that were already there, listed separately.
+- Proposals for Justin; files updated; the next action, written into lab `STATE.md`.
